# What must not reach the build context. Three kinds, and the middle one is the
# one that would be silently wrong:
#
# - build output that the image rebuilds anyway (`dbt/target`, `dbt_packages`,
#   `node_modules`, `reports/build`, `.venv`, `__pycache__`) — copying it in
#   would layer a host's artifacts under the ones the Dockerfile builds, and
#   invalidate `COPY . .` and every layer after it whenever the host recompiles.
#   Patterns are anchored at the context root, so a directory that can appear
#   at any depth needs `**/`: a bare `__pycache__` matched the root alone;
# - *state* (`data/`, `.dagster/`, `.env`) — a warehouse, a landing zone or a
#   password baked into an image that then gets pushed somewhere;
# - noise (`.git`, `docs/sessions`).

.git
.venv
.env
data
.dagster
dbt/target
dbt/dbt_packages
dbt/logs
reports/node_modules
reports/build
reports/.evidence
docs/sessions
**/__pycache__
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
